msgid "A complete example for a formats repository"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/configuration/dev-and-validate.md:179
msgid ""
"One file, at the root of a formats repository, configuring all three "
"commands:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/configuration/dev-and-validate.md:198
msgid ""
"Note the two `target_lists`. The top-level one is what a **real "
"extraction** searches for; `dev`'s is what the **repository's own tests**"
" search for. They are different questions, and a repository that "
"conflated them would have tests whose result depended on the user's day "
"job."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/configuration/dev-and-validate.md:202
msgid "Unknown keys are errors here too"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/configuration/dev-and-validate.md:204
msgid ""
"`dev.tagret_lists` fails, naming the full path of the key. The engine "
"parses these sections even though it never reads them, precisely so that "
"this rule reaches inside them: a misspelled setting that is silently "
"ignored configures nothing and reports nothing."
msgstr ""

